# Build-context ALLOWLIST for every repo-root build — every compose service with
# `context: ..` (all of them except smart-exporter, which builds from its own
# deploy/smart-exporter context). No per-Dockerfile `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` exists;
# adding one would REPLACE this file for that build, not merge with it.
#
# Rule: deny everything, re-include exactly the paths some Dockerfile COPYs, then re-deny
# the runtime data and toolchain junk that sits inside those trees (last match wins).
# A COPY source this file does not re-include fails the build with "not found", so when
# a Dockerfile gains a COPY — or a new workspace member joins the manifest ripple — add
# its path here too.
#
# ⚠ Every `!` re-include must be a LITERAL path — no `*`/`**`/`?`. A single wildcard
# exception stops the BuildKit client from pruning ANY excluded directory: it then walks
# all of artifacts/ (and fails outright on the uid-70 0700 Postgres data dir —
# "error from sender: open …/artifacts/postgres/dagster: permission denied"), plus
# .claude/worktrees and every node_modules. Verified with buildx 0.13 / Docker 25.
# Wildcards are fine in plain (deny) lines.
#
# Why an allowlist (0037 OPS-1/OPS-22/PIPE-5): the old deny-list let dagster/Dockerfile's
# `COPY apps/scribe` + `COPY apps/mouthpiece-backend` bake ~23 GB of Craig zips, session
# audio and rendered episodes into the Dagster image (25.7 GB). BuildKit only transfers
# the paths a Dockerfile names, so the rest of the 30 GB context (libs/rust target/,
# .claude/worktrees, deploy/sops/age.key) was never sent — but nothing kept it out of a
# future `COPY .` or whole-dir COPY either. Now the context is ~111 MB.
*

# --- Workspace roots: pnpm + uv manifests/lockfiles, the base tsconfig ---
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock

# --- Shared libraries + ontology (copied wholesale; libs/ts carries the committed
# weal-engine wasm under libs/ts/weal-engine/gen) ---
!libs/ts
!libs/py
!ontology

# --- TS apps copied wholesale (`COPY apps/<app>`, incl. the templated ARG APP builds) ---
!apps/akasha-frontend
!apps/codex
!apps/harrow
!apps/ledger
!apps/menhir
!apps/mouthpiece-frontend
!apps/orator-backend
!apps/portal/module
!apps/portal/shared
!apps/strider
!apps/vellum-frontend
!apps/vellum-render
!apps/weal-overlay

# --- TS apps copied in part (manifest + src/) ---
!apps/portal/headless/package.json
!apps/portal/headless/src
!apps/portal/server/package.json
!apps/portal/server/src
!apps/weal-bot/package.json
!apps/weal-bot/src

# --- Manifest-only member. Every TS Dockerfile copies EVERY pnpm member's package.json
# (the manifest ripple) so `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` reconciles; the members
# above are covered by their own lines, orator-controller is copied for nothing else. ---
!apps/orator-controller/package.json

# --- Python workspace members (dagster/Dockerfile: `uv sync --frozen` needs every
# uv.lock member present). ---
!apps/_smoke-substrate
!apps/akasha-backend
!apps/assay
!apps/heartwood-backend
!apps/linguist
!apps/mouthpiece-backend
!apps/scribe

# --- Dagster code location + instance config ---
!dagster/definitions.py
!dagster/dagster.yaml
!dagster/workspace.yaml

# ======================= Re-deny inside the re-included trees =======================

# Pipeline runtime data. All of it is bind-mounted into the Dagster services at run time
# (deploy/docker-compose.yml `x-dagster-volumes`), so an image copy is dead weight.
apps/scribe/incoming
apps/scribe/data
apps/scribe/tmp
apps/mouthpiece-backend/episodes
apps/linguist/script

# The published datasets' OLD in-tree paths (0037 Phase 1 item 2): they live in the
# astra-data repo now and the frontends bake them from the `astra-data` build context
# (compose additional_contexts), so no image may read a stale copy from this tree.
apps/linguist/transcripts
apps/linguist/data
apps/linguist/timeline
apps/mouthpiece-backend/snapshot
apps/akasha-backend/content
apps/akasha-backend/snapshot
apps/heartwood-backend/agent-runs.jsonl
ontology/ontology-entity/entity.kdl

# codex's fetched corpus + Pagefind index (~1.5 GB) — mounted read-only at run time
# (D29-53/54); the build is corpus-free.
apps/codex/data

# Regenerated by each frontend's own build (build-content in the vite buildStart hook),
# so the host's copies are stale by definition.
apps/*/src/generated/*
apps/akasha-frontend/public/static
apps/akasha-frontend/public/index.xml
apps/akasha-frontend/public/sitemap.xml
apps/mouthpiece-frontend/public/episodes.json

# Other gitignored output/scratch inside copied trees (codex/books is the host-only
# `assay export-book` LaTeX source; no build reads it).
apps/assay/out
apps/assay/review-ui/data.json
apps/assay/review-ui/state
apps/codex/books

# Toolchain output + caches — rebuilt in-image (node_modules via pnpm install, the venv
# via uv sync, dist/ via the app build) or irrelevant to any build.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/dist
**/.output
**/.nitro
**/.tanstack
**/.tsbuild
**/storybook-static
**/target
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.ty_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets never enter a build context. deploy/ (SOPS file + age.key) is never
# re-included; these catch strays inside the re-included trees.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.agekey
**/age.key
